\ Temporary safe day coordinates, including extreme opposite pairs.
\ These tests inspect bounds only: they do not invoke expensive
\ far-distant gate walks. Their purpose is to reject coordinates that
\ could overflow a signed 32-bit calculation count or counter sum.

To check native date coordinate bounds:
  Check native day coordinate inputs given -15055671 and -15055671.
  If the native date input validity is no,
    put "Foundation was rejected by native safety bounds." into the check report; exit.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given -415055671 and 384944329.
  If the native date input validity is no,
    put "The safe endpoints were incorrectly rejected." into the check report; exit.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given 384944329 and -415055671.
  If the native date input validity is no,
    put "The reversed safe endpoints were incorrectly rejected." into the check report; exit.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given -415055672 and -15055671.
  If the native date input validity is yes,
    put "An overflowing earlier day was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given -15055671 and 384944330.
  If the native date input validity is yes,
    put "An overflowing later day was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given 384944329 and -415055672.
  If the native date input validity is yes,
    put "A pair with one unsafe day was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Check native day coordinate inputs given 384944329 and 384944329.
  If the native date input validity is no,
    put "A later safe pair remained rejected after invalid input." into the check report; exit.
